  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Juba County Recovery, Reintgration and Sustainable Livelihoods Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a 5 months bridging gap project as CAFOD continues to finalise its Country Strategy Document and it builds upon lessons learnt from the previous cycle, and the findings and recommendations of the Sustainable Livelihoods Programme evaluation conducted in 2013.  This project will also build upon key findings of the Horn &amp; East Africa Think Small 2 (TS2) research.  Within the Horn &amp; East Africa region, the TS2 research was conducted specifically in Kenya and South Sudan.  In South Sudan, beneficiaries from Caritas Archdiocese of Juba were considered as sample for the South Sudan Livelihoods Programme.  The PPA household Economic Survey conducted in November 2013 also highlighted some improvements in the lives of beneficiaries we support, that is changing eating patterns, improved income, and increased access to extension services and agriculture inputs, however more need to be done if lasting positive impact is to happen to change the lives of these poor and vulnerable people. Furthermore, from April 7 &#x2013; 11th of 2014 the resilience and sustainability cluster gathered for the first time in Kitui Kenya to discuss the benefits of an integrated approach and share best practices and lessons learned from various projects and countries that CAFOD works in. Discussions within the Livelihoods theme had highlighted that it is not enough just to help poor and disadvantaged people to &#x2018;hang in&#x2019; to a subsistence livelihood, but that we should be looking beyond survival, to build livelihoods that enable poor people to thrive as well as survive.  This project is intended to address these outlined issues which as they sounds may not be achievable within this period but they have to be started.</narrative>
  </description>
